# receipt: first measure, 2026-11-09: three corpus programs on the tree-walker, chuuzou's host image and a hand-written Rust twin, CPU over Rust's
# receipt: 2026-11-10: chuuzou and Rust run at a big N (fib 38, loop 300M, shapes 100M); the tree-walker row is its CPU per unit of work over Rust's, so every earlier tree row was startup-bound and is replaced; shapes is new
# receipt: 2026-11-10: sums is new (a list of N words built by append and summed by nth, once refcounted and once in a region)
# receipt: 2026-11-10: the VM is a column (blue run --vm), gated per unit of work like the tree-walker; every path measured with a release build of this tree
# receipt: 2026-11-10: a decrement and a remainder that a range proves safe are plain operators (loop 1.61 -> 0.88 of Rust)
# receipt: platform: 2026-11-21: first linux rows, measured on rio (x86-64, 32 cores): every native path, and bluec (hashiru through gen/native-row.b, :run mode) for fib, loop and mutual; bluec refuses shapes (records) and sums (reclaim)
# receipt: un-gain: 2026-11-21: mutual's seven rows leave the gate. It has no N, so each path's time and Rust's are a process start of 0.2-0.6 ms and their ratio is noise (bluec linux read 1333, 3000 and 1500 on three runs of one build); a program with no N is still run and its output still held to the Rust twin's, it is only not timed against it
